MASTER DEVELOPMENT PROMPT
Beneficiary Nomination System – Workday-Inspired Enterprise Application
1. PROJECT OBJECTIVE
Build a complete, modern, responsive Beneficiary Nomination System using the existing SharePoint data structure and Power Automate workflows.
The application is intended for a financial services organisation and must provide an enterprise-grade user experience inspired by Workday.
CRITICAL REQUIREMENT: USE THE EXISTING ENTITIES.
Do not introduce alternative database entities, rename existing SharePoint lists, or create a new database architecture.
The application must work with the following four actual SharePoint entities:
schemes
principalOfficers
Nomination Members
Nomination Nominees
These are the source entities for the application.
Before implementing anything:
Inspect the existing project.
Inspect the SharePoint data source connections.
Inspect the actual columns and data types of all four entities.
Inspect the existing Power Automate integrations.
Identify lookup columns and relationships.
Understand how reference numbers are generated.
Identify the existing approval status values.
Preserve all existing backend functionality.
Never assume that a field exists simply because it appears in a UI requirement.
2. ACTUAL DATA ENTITIES AND THEIR PURPOSE
ENTITY 1: schemes
Purpose: Maintain pension funds and schemes available for employee beneficiary nominations.
Examples of existing schemes:
Telekom Networks
Magetsi Fund
Madzi Fund
Alimi Fund
Responsibilities:
Retrieve available schemes.
Display scheme information.
Allow administrators to create schemes.
Allow administrators to edit schemes.
Activate or deactivate schemes.
Associate schemes with their assigned Principal Officers.
Use the existing SharePoint columns and field types.
Do not introduce a second scheme table or duplicate scheme information in another entity.
ENTITY 2: principalOfficers
Purpose: Maintain Principal Officer information and scheme assignments.
Required information includes:
Full Name.
Email.
Contact Number.
Scheme Assignment.
Status.
Responsibilities:
Retrieve Principal Officers.
Display assigned schemes.
Create Principal Officers.
Edit Principal Officer information.
Disable Principal Officers.
Assign Principal Officers to schemes.
The Principal Officer dashboard must retrieve the logged-in officer's assignments from the existing entity.
Do not create a separate Principal Officer entity.
ENTITY 3: Nomination Members
Purpose: This is the main nomination header entity.
It stores employee/member information and represents an individual beneficiary nomination submission.
Information to display and capture includes:
Member Number.
Date of Birth.
Branch Code.
Cost Centre.
Email Address.
Fund Name.
Reference Number.
Submission Date.
Approval Status.
Uploaded Form Name.
Uploaded Form URL.
Important existing document fields:
SourceFileName
SourceFileUrl
The above are known functional fields. Inspect the actual SharePoint schema to establish the complete field names and internal column names before implementation.
Responsibilities:
Create nomination submissions.
Retrieve existing submissions.
Display submission details.
Search nominations.
Display uploaded document information.
Track approval status.
Retrieve records using Reference Number.
Display approval history where available through the existing backend.
Reference Number is the primary identifier for a nomination throughout the application.
Do not generate a second nomination identifier.
ENTITY 4: Nomination Nominees
Purpose: Store beneficiary details linked to employee nomination submissions.
The actual CSV export confirms the following fields:
Actual field	Purpose
Title	Beneficiary full name
Member	Existing member-related field
MemberNumber	Employee/member number
RowNumber	Existing row number
DateOfBirth	Beneficiary date of birth
Relationship	Relationship to member
IdentityNumber	National ID or identity number
BenefitCurrentPct	Existing benefit percentage
BenefitRevisedPct	Revised benefit percentage
FundName	Associated pension fund
refNumber	Nomination reference number
Use these actual field names when retrieving, displaying, and updating beneficiary information.
Do not replace them with invented fields such as:
BeneficiaryID.
NominationID.
AllocationPercentage.
EmployeeReference.
Where the UI requires a friendly label, map it to the actual field.
Examples:
Title → Beneficiary Full Name.
DateOfBirth → Date of Birth.
IdentityNumber → National ID / Identity Number.
BenefitRevisedPct → Revised Benefit Percentage.
refNumber → Reference Number.
IMPORTANT: Preserve both BenefitCurrentPct and BenefitRevisedPct.
Inspect the existing data and workflow to determine how these fields are used. Do not overwrite current percentages or assume that both fields have identical purposes.
The refNumber field links beneficiaries to the corresponding record in Nomination Members.
One nomination can have multiple beneficiaries.
Relationship:
Nomination Members.refNumber ↔ Nomination Nominees.refNumber
Use the actual SharePoint column types and lookup behaviour when implementing this relationship.
Treat reference numbers as identifiers, not mathematical values. Preserve their original representation when displaying or searching them.
